💭 Comparisons of reals when one side is not a number.
💭
💭 Expected: nothing but "done". IEEE 754 has every ordered comparison with a NaN false.
💭 What happens: all four lines are printed. The compiler emits LLVM's unordered
💭 comparisons (FCmpUEQ, FCmpULT, FCmpUGT …), each of which is true when either side is
💭 a NaN, so a NaN is equal to 0.0, below it and above it at once, and a loop that waits
💭 for a comparison to turn false never ends on one.
🏁 🍇
  0.0 ➡️ zero
  zero ➗ zero ➡️ nan
  ↪️ nan 🙌 0.0 🍇
    😀 🔤a NaN is equal to 0.0🔤❗️
  🍉
  ↪️ nan ◀️ 0.0 🍇
    😀 🔤a NaN is below 0.0🔤❗️
  🍉
  ↪️ nan ▶️ 0.0 🍇
    😀 🔤a NaN is above 0.0🔤❗️
  🍉
  ↪️ nan 🙌 nan ➕ 1.0 🍇
    😀 🔤a NaN is equal to itself and one more🔤❗️
  🍉
  😀 🔤done🔤❗️
